  "job_B1.4.11_20251001_193229": {
    "text": "We wylla\u00f0 eow secgan sume swutelunge nu be \u00feam halgum tidum \u00f0e we healda\u00f0 and weor\u00f0ia\u00f0 on\n\u00c6rest we wor\u00f0ia\u00f0 on Middewintres D\u00e6ge ures H\u00e6lendes acennednysse, hu he to mannum com on so\u00f0re\nOn \u00feam twelftan d\u00e6ge \u00fe\u00e6re tide ymbeganges we wur\u00f0ia\u00f0 mid lofsangum hu \u00f0a geleaffullan cyningas\nOn \u00feam feowerteogo\u00f0an d\u00e6ge fram his acennednysse, \u00f0e we cwe\u00f0a\u00f0 on Englisc Candelm\u00e6ssed\u00e6g, b\u00e6r\nOn Lengtenes anginne we eac swylce wur\u00f0ia\u00f0 mid urum lofsangum hu se leofa H\u00e6lend on \u00feam\nEft we weor\u00f0ia\u00f0 on ufeweardan Lengtene on halgum r\u00e6dingum \u00fe\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes \u00f0rowunge, hu he w\u00e6s\nHe aras eft of dea\u00f0e on \u00feam Easterd\u00e6ge, mid \u00feam ylcan lichaman \u00f0e he \u00e6r on \u00f0rowode to ecum\nOn \u00f0am feowerteogo\u00f0an d\u00e6ge \u00fe\u00e6s \u00f0e he of dea\u00f0e aras, he astah to heofonum to his halgan F\u00e6der, mid\nEft \u00f0\u00e6s ymbe tyn niht on urum \u00f0eowdome we m\u00e6rsia\u00f0 \u00feone d\u00e6g mid m\u00e6rlicum wur\u00f0mynte \u00fee we\nSeofon dagas we wur\u00f0ia\u00f0 mid urum sange on cyrcan \u00f0one halgan tocyme \u00fe\u00e6s Halgan Gastes, for \u00f0\u00e6re\nOn \u00f0yssere wucan we wur\u00f0odon \u00f0as tid, and nu tod\u00e6g we heria\u00f0 \u00fea halgan \u00ferynnysse mid urum\n\u00c6fre w\u00e6s se F\u00e6der witodlice mid \u00feam Suna, and eac se Halga Gast, on eallum his f\u00e6relde, for \u00f0an \u00f0e\nEall \u00f0\u00e6s geares ymbegang hera\u00f0 God \u00e6lmihtigne, and we mid urum \u00f0eowdome ge\u00f0w\u00e6rl\u00e6ca\u00f0 \u00feam\nSe frumsceapena mann, swa swa we s\u00e6don eow oft, Adam ure f\u00e6der, w\u00e6s \u00f0urh God swa gesceapen\n\u00d0a com se ealda deofol mid andan afylled, and beswac \u00f0one mann, \u00fe\u00e6t he syngode wi\u00f0 God, and his\nNe gesceop God \u00feone dea\u00f0, ne he so\u00f0lice ne blissa\u00f0 on manna forwyrde, swa swa gewritu secga\u00f0.\nInuidia autem diaboli mors intrauit in orbem terrarum: Ac \u00f0urh \u00fe\u00e6s deofles andan se dea\u00f0 com on \u00f0as\nOn \u00f0reo wisan he cym\u00f0, swa swa hit fullcu\u00f0 is: Mors acerba, mors inmatura, mors naturalis; \u00f0\u00e6t is on\nSe bitera dea\u00f0 is gecweden \u00fee bi\u00f0 on cildum, and se ungeripoda dea\u00f0, on geongum mannum, and se\n\u00c6lc man him ondr\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6s lichaman dea\u00f0, and feawa him ondr\u00e6da\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6re sawle dea\u00f0.\n\u00deam lichaman men tilia\u00f0, \u00fee lange lybban ne m\u00e6g, and ne tilia\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6re sawle \u00fee ne swelt on ecnysse.\nNe becym\u00f0 na yfel dea\u00f0 \u00feam \u00f0e \u00e6r wel lyfode, ac se h\u00e6f\u00f0 yfelne dea\u00f0 \u00f0e \u00feam dea\u00f0e folgode, and on\nNe \u00f0earft \u00f0u na hogian hu \u00f0u sceole sweltan, ac hoga \u00f0u swi\u00f0or hu \u00f0in sawol sceole \u00e6fter \u00feam\nTwegen dea\u00f0as synd, swa swa us secga\u00f0 bec: an is \u00f0\u00e6s lichaman dea\u00f0, \u00fee eallum mannum becym\u00f0,\n\u00deysum dea\u00f0e \u00e6twinda\u00f0, swa swa ure Drihten cw\u00e6\u00fe, \u00f0a \u00f0e his word healda\u00f0, and hi habba\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t ece lif\n\u00c6lc man \u00f0e Godes freond is sceolde swy\u00f0e \u00e6fstan \u00e6fre mid godum weorcum, \u00fe\u00e6t he Gode\nHwa dorste \u00e6fre gewilnian \u00fe\u00e6s wynsuman eardes, and swa miceles wur\u00f0myntes, gif se welwillenda\nMicel heap andbida\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r ura holdra freonda ures tocymes to him, hohfull git embe us, orsorh be him\nHwa nele nu efstan to \u00f0\u00e6re ecan blisse fram \u00feyssere earfo\u00f0nysse \u00f0e we on wunia\u00f0, fram deofles\nIs swa\u00f0eah micel neod \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0a \u00f0e manegum fremia\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t heora lif beo \u00fe\u00e6s \u00f0e leng mid us, and mid\nSe syrwienda deofol swica\u00f0 \u00e6fre embe us, and on \u00fe\u00e6s mannes for\u00f0si\u00f0e fela cnottan him bryt; ac se\nMan sceal eac syllan \u00feam seocan men husel, \u00fea hwile \u00f0e he hit \u00feicgan m\u00e6g, \u00e6r \u00f0am \u00f0e he sawlige, for\nTo goddra manna for\u00f0si\u00f0e God asent his englas, \u00fe\u00e6t hi heora sawla onfon on heora for\u00f0si\u00f0e, and\n\u00d0a \u00f0e gode beo\u00f0, and Gode \u00e6r gecwemdon, on eallum godum weorcum, \u00f0a wunia\u00f0 mid Gode, and \u00f0a\n\u00d0a fordonan synfullan \u00fee deofle gehyrsumodon on eallum synnum, and forsawon heora Drihten, and\nGif se man wolde huru, \u00feonne he seoc bi\u00f0, to Gode gecyrran, and his synna geandettan mid so\u00f0re\nNis na eallum mannum se gem\u00e6nelica dea\u00f0 gelice earfo\u00f0e, ac foroft becym\u00f0 \u00feam synfullan men\nSume eac blissia\u00f0 on heora for\u00f0si\u00f0e foroft, \u00feonne hi witodlice geseo\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t hi sceolon to reste, and\nSumera manna sawla si\u00f0ia\u00f0 to reste \u00e6fter heora for\u00f0si\u00f0e, and sume fara\u00f0 to witum, be \u00feam \u00f0e hi\nSeo sawul h\u00e6f\u00f0 so\u00f0lice, swa swa us secga\u00f0 bec, \u00fe\u00e6s lichaman gelicnysse on eallum hyre limum, and\nSume leahtras beo\u00f0 on \u00f0isum life gebette, and sume \u00e6fter dea\u00f0e, swa swa ure Drihten s\u00e6de; ac \u00f0a\n\u00d0a leohtan gyltas and \u00f0a lytlan synna beo\u00f0 \u00feonne afeormode \u00feurh \u00f0\u00e6t witniendlice fyr, and nis nanes\nSume beo\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r lange, sume lytle hwile, be \u00feam \u00f0e him fore beo\u00f0 his frynd her on life, and be \u00feam \u00f0e\nAnd \u00fea halgan sawla \u00fee on heofonum wunia\u00f0 gebidda\u00f0 for us \u00f0e on eor\u00f0an wunia\u00f0, and eac for \u00f0am\n\u00dea halgan sawla syndon so\u00f0lice on blisse, on anfealdum gyrlum \u00fe\u00e6re ecan blisse, for \u00f0an \u00f0e hi lybba\u00f0\nD\u00e6ghwamlice hi willnia\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t Domesd\u00e6g cume hra\u00f0e, \u00fe\u00e6t hi magon blissian on twyfealdre blisse, on\nNu hi sceawia\u00f0 so\u00f0lice heora Scyppendes beorhtnysse, and nis for\u00f0i nan gesceaft \u00fee hi geseon ne\n\u00dea halgan sawla geseo\u00f0 swutollice ealle \u00f0ing, ac \u00f0a arleasan sawla \u00f0e on suslum wunia\u00f0 ne magon\nNis nanum men nu cu\u00f0, ne cucum ne deadum, ne nanum gesceafte, swa swa se H\u00e6lend s\u00e6de, Hwenne\nUre H\u00e6lend s\u00e6de him sylf be \u00feam d\u00e6ge \u00fe\u00e6t woruldmen bytlia\u00f0 and bega\u00f0 heora tilunge, and\nUnderstanda\u00f0 nu, men, hu micel miht is on Criste, \u00feonne seo sunne and se mona ne magon syllan nan\nEngla werod bera\u00f0 \u00fea beorhtan rode him \u00e6tforan, and his slagan geseo\u00f0 hw\u00e6ne hi ofslogon \u00e6r, and he\n\u00d0onne oferg\u00e6\u00fe an fyr ealle \u00f0as woruld, and se engel bl\u00e6w\u00f0 \u00fea seofo\u00f0an byman, \u00fe\u00e6t is seo \u00e6ftemyste,\n\u00d0a cucan beo\u00f0 ofslagene sona mid \u00feam fyre, ac hi beo\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6rrihte eft acucode on ecum lichaman, swa\n\u00c6lc man h\u00e6f\u00f0 swa\u00f0eah his agene lenge, on \u00f0\u00e6re mycelnysse \u00fee he man w\u00e6s \u00e6r, o\u00f0\u00f0e he beon\nSwa swa God gesceop on sawle and on lichaman ge w\u00e6pmen ge wifmen, and geworhte hi to men, and\nNe \u00f0a halgan ne beo\u00f0 \u00fee to heofonum sceolon on \u00e6nigre awyrdnysse, o\u00f0\u00f0e wanhale, o\u00f0\u00f0e anegede,\n\u00d0a wi\u00f0ercorenan so\u00f0lice, \u00f0e wunia\u00f0 \u00e6fre on suslum, hw\u00e6t sceal him \u00e6nig wlite on \u00feam sweartan\n\u00c6lc man sceal arisan \u00feonne \u00fee \u00e6fre on life w\u00e6s; w\u00e6re he on w\u00e6tere adruncen, o\u00f0\u00f0e hine wilde deor\nMan bewint \u00feone deadan gewunelice mid reafe, ac \u00f0\u00e6t reaf ne arist na \u00f0e hra\u00f0or mid \u00feam men, for\nGod asent \u00feonne his englas, and hi gegaderia\u00f0 him to ealle his gecorenan of eallum middanearde, and\n\u00deonne sitt se H\u00e6lend on his heofonlican \u00f0rymsetle, mihtig and wuldorful, and milde \u00feam godum,\nHis twelf apostolas, \u00fee him folgodon on life, sitta\u00f0 \u00feonne eac on twelf domsettlum, and ealle \u00f0a\n\u00d0\u00e6r beo\u00f0 feower gefylcu on \u00feam micelan flocce: \u00fe\u00e6t forme gefylc bi\u00f0 \u00fee we her fores\u00e6don, \u00fee sitta\u00f0\n\u00d0\u00e6t o\u00f0er werod bi\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6ra woruldmanna \u00f0e on godum weorcum Gode \u00e6r gecwemdon, and mid\n\u00d0\u00e6t \u00feridde werod bi\u00f0 witodlice \u00feonne \u00fe\u00e6ra Cristenra manna \u00f0e cu\u00f0on heora geleafan, ac hi gremedon\n\u00de\u00e6t feor\u00f0e gefylc bi\u00f0 \u00f0\u00e6ra fulra h\u00e6\u00f0enra \u00fee nane cy\u00f0\u00f0e ne h\u00e6fdon to \u00feam heofonlican Gode, ne\nNe m\u00e6g \u00feonne nan man nahwar beon behydd, ac ealle beo\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r \u00fee \u00e6fre cuce w\u00e6ron, and \u00fe\u00e6r beo\u00f0\n\u00de\u00e6r beo\u00f0 ealle gelice, ge se hlaford ge se \u00f0eowa, se rica and se heana, on \u00feam rihtan dome, and \u00f0\u00e6r\n\u00d0onne cwe\u00f0 se H\u00e6lend of his halgan \u00f0rymsettle to \u00f0am godum Cristenum \u00f0e Godes willan\nMe hingrode so\u00f0lice, and ge me gereordodon.\nEft \u00f0a \u00f0a me \u00feyrste, ge sealdon me drincan.\nEac ic w\u00e6s cuma, and ge me underfengon.\nIc w\u00e6s eac swilce nacod, and ge me scryddon.\nIc w\u00e6s eac swilce untrum, and ge me geneosodon.\nOn cwearterne ic w\u00e6s, and ge comon to me.\n\u00deonne andswaria\u00f0 hi \u00f0am arf\u00e6stan Deman \u00feus: Eala \u00f0u Drihten leof, hw\u00e6nne gesawe we \u00f0e o\u00f0\u00f0e\nO\u00f0\u00f0e hw\u00e6nne w\u00e6re \u00f0u cuma and we \u00f0e underfengon, o\u00f0\u00f0e hw\u00e6nne w\u00e6re \u00feu unscryd and we \u00f0e\nHw\u00e6nne w\u00e6re \u00feu untrum and we \u00f0e geneosodon, o\u00f0\u00f0e on cwearterne and we comon to \u00f0e?\n\u00d0onne andwyrt se Cyning \u00feam arf\u00e6stan and cwe\u00f0: So\u00f0 ic eow secge, \u00fe\u00e6t ge me sylfum dydon \u00feas\n\u00de\u00e6t is so\u00f0lice swa to understandenne: swa oft swa ge \u00e6lmessan dydon anum lytlan \u00f0earfan of\n\u00d0onne cwe\u00f0 se Dema eft to \u00f0am dreorigan heape \u00f0e stent on his wynstran hand, Gewita\u00f0 heonan fram\nMe hingrode so\u00f0lice, and ge me ne gereordodon; eft ic w\u00e6s \u00f0urstig, and ge me ne scencton.\nEac ic w\u00e6s cuma, and ge me ne underfengon; ic w\u00e6s eac swilce unscryd; nolde ge me scrydan.\nIc w\u00e6s untrum and on cwearterne; ne come ge to me.\n\u00deonne andwyrda\u00f0 \u00fea synfullan \u00feam so\u00f0an Deman \u00f0us: Eala \u00f0u so\u00f0a Drihten, hw\u00e6nne gesawe we \u00f0e\n\u00d0onne andwyrt se Dema \u00feam earmum forscyldegodum: So\u00f0 ic eow secge, me sylfum ge his\n\u00d0onne gewita\u00f0 \u00fea earmingas and \u00f0a arleasan synfullan into \u00feam ecan wite mid \u00feam awyrgedan\nOn \u00f0isum wordum we magon gewislice tocnawan \u00f0\u00e6t \u00f0a synfullan beo\u00f0 besencte \u00e6rest on helle, mid\nBe \u00f0\u00e6re ylcan endebyrdnysse awrat eac Iohannes \u00f0us: Heora \u00e6lcum w\u00e6s gedemed be his agenum\nSe dea\u00f0 and seo hell is se deofol sylf, for \u00f0an \u00f0e he is ealdor \u00f0\u00e6s ecan dea\u00f0es, and he is se ordfruma\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 eft Iohannes be \u00f0am arleasum mannum: \u00e6lc \u00f0\u00e6ra manna w\u00e6s aworpen into \u00f0am widgillan\nOn anum fyre hi byrna\u00f0 on \u00feam byrnendan mere, \u00f0a earman menniscan menn, and \u00f0a modigan deoflu;\nNu smeaga\u00f0 sume men hu \u00f0a unges\u00e6ligan deoflu magon \u00f0\u00e6r gefredan \u00f0\u00e6s fyres bryne on him, \u00feonne\nWe secga\u00f0 nu to so\u00fean \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0\u00e6s mannes sawul is belocen on his lichaman \u00f0a hwile \u00f0e he lybbende\nEall swa ea\u00f0elice m\u00e6g se \u00e6lmihtiga God belucan \u00f0a deofla on \u00feam deorcan fyre, \u00fe\u00e6t hi \u00f0\u00e6ron\n\u00d0\u00e6ra manna wite bi\u00f0 swa gemetegod \u00feurh God \u00fe\u00e6t se \u00f0e hwonlicor syngode, \u00fe\u00e6t he hwonlicor\n\u00d0\u00e6t li\u00f0oste wite and \u00fe\u00e6t leohtoste bi\u00f0 \u00f0am unwittigum cildum \u00f0e w\u00e6ron ungefullode, \u00fee nane o\u00f0re\nNe magon \u00fea fordemdan, ne fur\u00f0on \u00f0a deoflu, \u00fea blisse geseon \u00fee bi\u00f0 mid \u00f0am halgum, sy\u00f0\u00f0an hi\nIohannes se Godspellere, on his gastlican gesih\u00f0e, cw\u00e6\u00fe \u00fe\u00e6t he gesawe sy\u00f0\u00f0an \u00e6fter \u00f0isum, eallniwe\n\u00c6fter \u00f0ysum dome ure Drihten f\u00e6r\u00f0 to his heofonlican F\u00e6der, mid \u00feam halgum mannum \u00f0e he on\nCrist him gel\u00e6st \u00feonne, swa swa he him on life behet, \u00f0a \u00f0a he clypode of eor\u00f0an to his \u00e6lmihtigan\nSe H\u00e6lend so\u00f0lice is his halgena heafod, and hi mid him rixia\u00f0, his englum gelice, and hi God geseo\u00f0,\nAnd eft se apostol Paulus on his pistole cw\u00e6\u00f0: Nu we menn geseo\u00f0 swilce \u00feurh sceawere, and on\nEft cw\u00e6\u00fe se H\u00e6lend on his halgan godspelle, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0\u00e6r ic sylf beo, \u00f0\u00e6r bi\u00f0 min \u00f0en, and se \u00f0e me\nManega becuma\u00f0 of middanearde to heofonum Godes halgena, for \u00f0an \u00f0e he habban wile micel werod\n\u00d0\u00e6r bi\u00f0 swi\u00f0e micel and swi\u00f0e m\u00e6re on wuldre se \u00fee l\u00e6st bi\u00f0 ge\u00f0uht on \u00feam life wunigende, and he\n\u00c6lc man m\u00e6g \u00f0\u00e6r geseon o\u00f0res mannes ge\u00f0oht, ne him n\u00e6fre ne hingra\u00f0, ne hefigmod ne bi\u00f0, ne him\nHe is heora rice, and lif, and wur\u00f0mynt, heora h\u00e6l and wuldor, sibb and genihtsumnys, and \u00f0\u00e6r\nSe \u00f0e leofa\u00f0 and rixa\u00f0 mid his leofan Suna and \u00f0am Halgan gaste, on anre godcundnysse, an \u00e6lmihtig",
